    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:936a34ccc6e7c635",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2edcf210ad85d55fc96046d972364567622a0655d48d9888123f343ed8310a47",
      "text": "Day 14 · Drive towards the Peruvian border and Lake Titicaca, visiting on the way the majestic ruins of Tiwanaku (c. 1580 BC – AD 1000), one of the oldest civilisations in South America: the Gate of the Sun, the Kalasasaya Temple and the pyramids. Skilled in agriculture, hydraulics, architecture, medicine and social organisation, the Tiwanaku culture collapsed at the end of the first millennium AD, after natural disasters including long droughts.\n\nIn the afternoon, visit the floating Uros Islands, built of reeds, with an English-speaking guide. Their inhabitants have preserved their traditional way of life, customs, beliefs and dress. Overnight in Puno.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1D9b9CT24BvopVtwbWVZClhDY4V-81Q5M",
